SQSO-JET-BRD-001 electrical rule check (SKiDL 3.0 ERC), generated by design.py

No errors or warnings found while running ERC.


Waivers (intentional modelling choices, reviewed):
W1  Connector pins (J1-J6) are PASSIVE; the module socket J4 carries the module's own drivers (POWER_EN is a
    module input, SYS_RESET* and SHUTDOWN_REQ* are module open-drain outputs with module pull-ups, the UARTs
    are 1.8 V CMOS): nets driven only through J4 are correct.
W2  Power nets fed through passive elements (connector, filter inductor, buck inductors, damper) are declared
    driven (net.drive = POWER): VBAT_IN, VBAT_F, DAMP, 5V_BUCK, 3V3_PRE, JET_3V3.
W3  Pins marked NOCONNECT are open on purpose: PGOOD of U1 and U3 (not used: U2 PG and the module's own
    sequence govern), the NC pins of U6, U9, U12 and the ESD arrays, every module pin not in MODULE_USE (no
    camera, display, USB 1/2, USB 3.2, GbE, CAN, I2S, SPI, PCIe 1-3, PMIC_BBAT, CLK_32K_OUT, SLEEP/WAKE*;
    DS-11105-001 4.4), the unused M.2 pins (lanes 1-3, DEVSLP, SMBus, SUSCLK, PEDET) and the isolated
    mounting holes H1-H6.
W4  POWER_EN has three open-drain/open-collector drivers (U2 PG, U4 RESET) and one pull-up: a wired AND.
W5  PT_NTC/PT_RTN connect only passives (RT1, J2, J3, D2): the OBC biases and reads the thermistor.
